DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These  functions  provide a conversion between 32‐bit long integers and
       little‐endian base‐64 ASCII strings (of length zero to  six).   If  the
       string  used  as  argument for aa6644ll() has length greater than six, only
       the first six bytes are used.  If the type _l_o_n_g has more than 32  bits,
       then  ll6644aa() uses only the low order 32 bits of _v_a_l_u_e, and aa6644ll() sign‐
       extends its 32‐bit result.

       The 64 digits in the base‐64 system are:

              '.'  represents a 0
              '/'  represents a 1
              0‐9  represent  2‐11
              A‐Z  represent 12‐37
              a‐z  represent 38‐63

       So 123 = 59*64^0 + 1*64^1 = "v/".

